 Bay Area Hengqin Guangdong-Macao in-depth cooperation zone Overview of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area Tourism Education and Training Base for the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area The Alliance for Developing Macao into the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area Tourism Education and Training Base Tourism Professional Education Alliance of Greater Bay Area Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao University Tourism Research Alliance Extension of Macao Base One Examination Multiple Certificates Press Release Adjunct Position of Institute of Executive and Professional Development (IEPD) Home Job Vacancies Adjunct Position of Institute of Executive and Professional Development (IEPD) The Institute of Executive and Professional Development ( IEPD) of Macao University of Tourism invites\napplications for the following adjunct teaching posts. Successful candidates are required to teach in Chinese and/or English for both daytime and evening programmes/courses: Adjunct Instructor(s) i n the subject area(s) of: AIGC Certificate Art Therapy Arts Creation Arts Management Bakery Chef Barista Bartender Business Data Analysis Cantonese Dim Sum Chinese Chef (Cantonese Cuisine) Chinese Chef (Dim Sum) Chinese Language Chinese Writing Classical Opera Communications Concierge and Bell Attendant Culture Culture and Skills of Weiqi Customer Relations Officer Digital Marketing Education Education and Assessment Education Management Entertainment Management ESG, including AA1000 ACSAP and CESGA Event Coordination and Planning Event Expert Event Production Financial Planning and Business Practices Financial Planning and Wealth Management, including AFP and CFP Floral Designer Food Nutrition, Hygiene and Science (must be authorized tutor for Servsafe® Food Protection Manager Certification course) French Front Desk Agent German Healthcare Heritage Hotel Management Hotel Security & Loss Prevention Management Information Technology Insurance Planning Investment Planning Japanese Korean Law Law and Theories of Cyber Security Livestreaming in E-commerce Lodging Operations Luxurious Product Management Macanese Cuisine Mandala Mindful Painting Marketing Strategies Media Creation, Operation and Management Mobile Technologies and Social Media in Hospitality Industry Modern Finance Music Ocean Engine Professional Certification Pastry Chef Portuguese Psychology Purchasing in Hospitality Retail Buying and Merchandising Retail Operations Retail Sales Officer Revenue Management Room Attendant Russian Screenwriting and Directing for Film Spanish Sport Sustainable Marketing Tea Master Thai Tourism Waiter/Waitress (Chinese Restaurant Service) Waiter/Waitress (Western Restaurant Service) Western Chef WorldSkills -- Hotel Reception Requirements: applicant must 1) be at least a secondary graduate; and 2) either possess certificates of related professional training with duration not less than 2 years, or with industry working experience in the relevant area. Applicants should apply online, select the relevant subject area(s) under \"IEPD \" and upload the required documents in PDF format at our Academic Recruitment Management System (ARMS) Applications that do not meet the “Requirements” or without provision of supporting documents or certificates will not be accepted. This recruitment is open until the positions are filled. Submitted applications are valid within one year after submission. Remark: for candidates who registered in our ARMS before 10 March 2023 are required to reset password to reactivate/enter into our new version of ARMS. Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used for recruitment purpose only. For enquiries, please send to this email . Home About UTM General Information Mission Statement UTM Council Rector Message Recognitions Organisational Law & General Rules of UTM Staff Annual Report UTM Videos Our Campus Access to UTM Taxi Card Campus Map Green Campus UTM Campus Visit First Phase of Macao-Hengqin Internatio