    "https://www.utm.edu.mo/visitors/job-vacancies/academic-positions/rector-of-macao-university-of-tourism-(ref.-no.-001-rec-ro-2026)": {
      "title": "Rector of Macao University of Tourism (Ref. no. 001/REC-RO/2026)",
      "description": "Rector of Macao University of Tourism (Ref. no. 001/REC-RO/2026) This website uses cookies to ensure you get the best experience on our website. Learn more Got it! Students Prospective Students Current Students Honour List Staff Staff Portal Student Information eServices Short Courses eServices Moodle Webmail Venue Booking Alumni Alumni Community Graduates Partners Job Posting for Alumni Job Posting for Students Graduate Verification Professional course certificate inquiry Platform Suppliers Database Public Tender Consulta Escrita Media News Portal Press Release Events Visitors New Professional/ Vocational/ Short Courses Job Vacancies Venues for Meeting & Event Location of UTM Explore UTM UTM Campus Virtual Tour Contact Us Contact Us Suggestions and Comments Enquiry Form English English 繁體 简体 Português About UTM General Information Mission Statement UTM Council Rector Message Recognitions Organisational Law & General Rules of UTM Staff Annual Report UTM Videos Our Campus First Phase of Macao-Hengqin International Education (University) Town Teaching Site Explore UTM Open Day Quality Assurance Policy Public Services and Organizational Performance Appraisal System Souvenirs Teaching & Learning Programmes Macao Higher Education Policies and Regulations Faculty of Innovative Hospitality Management Faculty of Creative Tourism and Intelligent Technologies Institute of Executive and Professional Development Centre for Education Quality Management Global Centre for Tourism Education and Training UTM-CRCS Centre for Innovative Talent Development Facilities Training Units We Care Ideation Lab iRetail Lab Admission Postgraduate Programmes Undergraduate Programmes Scholarships & Fellowships Global Exposure Information Guide for Non-local Students Research International Centre for Tourism and Hospitality Research Academic Publication Tourism Education Student Summit Global Network Introduction Membership Global Partners Global Exposure Greater Bay Area Hengqin Guangdong-Macao in-depth cooperation zone Overview of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area Tourism Education and Training Base for the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area The Alliance for Developing Macao into the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area Tourism Education and Training Base Tourism Professional Education Alliance of Greater Bay Area Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao University Tourism Research Alliance Extension of Macao Base One Examination Multiple Certificates Press Release Rector of Macao University of Tourism (Ref. no. 001/REC-RO/2026) Home Job Vacancies Rector of Macao University of Tourism (Ref. no. 001/REC-RO/2026) Recruitment of Rector of Macao University of Tourism New (Reference No. 001/REC-RO/2026) The Macao University of Tourism (UTM), established in 1995, is a public university in Macao. UTM offers degree programmes, as well as professional training in a wide range of culture, tourism and hospitality management related disciplines such as hospitality, tourism, cultural and heritage, creative and cultural studies, events, leisure and entertainment, sports and recreation, culinary arts, food and beverage, smart technologies, business, marketing and brand, communication, and language. UTM is committed to providing quality tourism education to its students, while striving to become a globally recognised higher education institution of excellence in tourism. UTM was the first institution accredited by the UN Tourism.TedQual Certification System for tourism education. The University has achieved prominent position in QS World University Rankings by Subject “Hospitality & Leisure Management”. It has been recognised as one of the best higher education institutions worldwide in tourism management. UTM focuses on the holistic development of its students, striving to enhance their competitiveness and entrepreneurship skills. For more information about UTM, please visit https://www.utm.edu.mo/. To implement the Macao SAR Government’s policy objectives of “Education to Prosper Macao and Talents to Shape Macao”, and to align with the international development of higher education, UTM has been advancing internationalisation through its educational provision, expanding its international student body and teaching team, and contributing to Macao’s development into a hub for high-calibre international talent. In accordance with the relevant provisions of the personnel ordinance of UTM, the UTM Council launches a global recruitment for the position of Rector. Major Responsibilities: To lead the academic and administrative management of the Macao University of Tourism; To ensure that the University fulfils its objectives and discharges its duties; To formulate the University’s overall policies and development plans, and submit them to the University Council for approval; To oversee the operation of academic units, training units and support units, and ensure coordination among them; To formulate the University’s annual activity plan and submit it to the University Council for consideration; To prepare the University’s annual activity report; To propose the creation, modification, suspension and discontinuation of higher education programmes in light of the University’s long-term development needs and financial viability; To strive to enhance the quality of teaching and research; To actively foster cooperation with renowned universities and industry organisations in Mainland China and overseas, thereby supporting the University in achieving its internationalisation goals; To strengthen industry-academia-research collaboration, enhance the University’s capacity for social services, and increase its social impact. Candidates Should Meet the Following Essential Requirements: Possess a doctoral degree; Be a Full Professor of a higher education institution, or possess substantial professional experience and recognised professional qualifications in the field of education; Be of good civic character. Preferred Requirements: At least eight years of teaching and academic research experience as a professor, or in a position equivalent to professor, in disciplines related to cultural tourism and hospitality management, with significant contributions to teaching and academic research; Not less than ten years of administrative management experience in higher education, preferably with experience serving as a vice-rector, dean, or in an equivalent position; Extensive networks in the academic, higher education, cultural tourism and hospitality professional fields, and the public sector at both global and national levels; preference will be given to candidates currently or previously holding key positions in such institutions; Familiarity with, and research experience in, economic development strategies relating to the cross-sector integration of cultural tourism and hospitality with other industries, as well as the transfer of research outcomes; ability to promote interdisciplinary integration and development within the University; Familiarity with development trends in higher education in Macao, Mainland China and overseas, with an international outlook and a forward-looking philosophy of university governance; Forward-looking thinking and outstanding leadership abilities, with the capacity to lead the University in achieving substantial development in teaching, research, internationalisation and social services; Fluency in Chinese and English for communication and professional exchange. Taxable Remuneration and Benefits: The university will offer a competitive salary based on the appointee's qualifications and relevant professional experience. Currently, the professional tax rate in Macao ranges from 7% to 12%. In addition, the university provides comprehensive benefits, including provident fund, housing allowance, family allowance, holiday allowance, and medical benefits, among others. Application Procedure: UTM has appointed Asianet Consultants (H.K.) Limited to provide consultancy services for the recruitment of this position. Applicants or persons wishing to nominate candidates for this position should submit an application letter, a detailed curriculum vitae in English and other relevant documents as early as possible before the application deadline to the address below, quoting the reference number 001/REC-RO/2026: Address: Room 05, 29/F, Infinitus Plaza, 199 Des Voeux Road Central, Central, Hong Kong Email: utm@asianetconsultants.com For enquiries, please contact Mr. Peter Liu at +852 2530 0130. Application closes on 26 October 2026 (Macao time) Applicants who are not invited for an interview within three months after submission of their applications may consider their applications unsuccessful. Personal data provided by applicants will be kept confidential and used only for recruitment purposes. Preference will be given to Macao permanent residents with equal qualifications and experience. Home About UTM General Information Mission Statement UTM Council Rector Message Recognitions Organisational Law & General Rules of UTM Staff Annual Report UTM Videos Our Campus Access to UTM Taxi Card Campus Map Green Campus UTM Campus Visit First Phase of Macao-Hengqin International Education (University) Town Teaching Site Explore UTM Open Day Quality Assurance Policy Public Services and Organizational Performance Appraisal System Service Items & Service Quality Standard Report of User Satisfaction Survey Report of Handling Suggestions, Complaints & Objections Report of Target Implementation Certificate of Recognition of the UTM Business Continuity Management System Policy Souvenirs Teaching & Learning Programmes Macao Higher Education Policies and Regulations Faculty of Innovative Hospitality Management Faculty of Creative Tourism and Intelligent Technologies Institute of Executive and Professional Development Centre for Education Quality Management Global Centre for Tourism Education and Training UTM-CRCS Centre for Innovative Talent Development Facilities Barrier Free Facilities Training Units We Care Ideation Lab iRetail Lab Admission Postgraduate Programmes Undergraduate Programmes Scholarships & Fellowships Global Exposure Information Guide for Non-local Students Research International Centre for Tourism and Hospitality Research Academic Publication Tourism Education Student Summit Global Network Introduction Membership Global Partners Global Exposure Greater Bay Area Hengqin Guangdong-Macao in-depth cooperation zone Overview of the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area Tourism Education and Training Base for the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area Macao University of Tourism (UTM) as the Relying Unit Relation Chart with Partners The Alliance for Developing Macao into the Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao Greater Bay Area Tourism Education and Training Base Tourism Professional Education Alliance of Greater Bay Area Guangdong-Hong Kong-Macao University Tourism Research Alliance Extension of Macao Base One Examination Multiple Certificates Press Release Students Prospective Students Current Students Academic Calendar Support services for students with disabilities Honour List Staff Staff Portal Student Information eServices Short Courses eServices Moodle Webmail Venue Booking Alumni Alumni Community Graduates Graduation Ceremony Rundown of Graduation Ceremony Demonstration on Proper Wearing of Graduation Gown Collection of Graduation Documents Other Items Partners Job Posting for Alumni Job Posting for Students Graduate Verification Professional course certificate inquiry Platform Suppliers Database List of Accepted Suppliers Public Tender Consulta Escrita Media News Portal Press Release Events Visitors New Professional/ Vocational/ Short Courses Job Vacancies Venues for Meeting & Event Meeting Room Location of UTM Explore UTM UTM Campus Virtual Tour Contact Us Contact Us Suggestions and Comments Enquiry Form WHAT'S NEW Event Privacy Policy Campus Life Career Prospects and Further Study UTM Lib